Post-adapter — runs AFTER upstream's all_of_them.patch. Restores
Haybarn-specific values that 00-haybarn-engine-adapter.patch
temporarily rewrote to make upstream's patch apply cleanly.

extension_install_info.hpp:
  After upstream's patch flips http://*.duckdb.org → https://*.duckdb.org,
  we put the Haybarn URL constants back and restore the long
  doc-comment explaining the R2 layout. Drops the
  CORE_NIGHTLY_REPOSITORY_URL constant we temporarily re-introduced
  (the haybarn engine intentionally has no nightly channel).

extension_load.cpp:
  Upstream's patch removes the EndsWith error block entirely (the
  wasm-loadable path doesn't need a filename gatekeeper), so the
  "DuckDB extensions" string the pre-adapter briefly introduced no
  longer exists in the source after upstream runs.

  Upstream's patch also ADDS a wasm-only hardcoded fallback URL
  (`https://extensions.duckdb.org`) inside `#ifdef
  WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS` in `TryInitialLoad`. This is the URL the
  wasm runtime uses when no `CustomExtensionRepository` setting is
  set, so extension auto-install (e.g. parquet, json) hits it on
  first call. Flip it to the Haybarn R2 core repository so signed
  Haybarn extensions actually resolve.

If/when the haybarn engine drops the Haybarn-specific doc comment or
the URLs move out of this file, this patch can be simplified or
deleted.

diff --git a/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_install_info.hpp b/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_install_info.hpp
--- a/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_install_info.hpp
+++ b/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_install_info.hpp
@@ -54,10 +54,29 @@
 };

 struct ExtensionRepository {
-	//! All currently available repositories
-	static constexpr const char *CORE_REPOSITORY_URL = "https://extensions.duckdb.org";
-	static constexpr const char *CORE_NIGHTLY_REPOSITORY_URL = "https://nightly-extensions.duckdb.org";
-	static constexpr const char *COMMUNITY_REPOSITORY_URL = "https://community-extensions.duckdb.org";
+	//! All currently available repositories. Haybarn hosts its own signed
+	//! extension repositories on Cloudflare R2, fronted by the single
+	//! `haybarn-extensions.query.farm` custom domain. Core and community share
+	//! one bucket, segregated by top-level path prefix (/core, /community).
+	//! The upstream nightly repository concept is intentionally dropped.
+	//!
+	//! https:// is mandatory for the wasm build: the browser performs each
+	//! extension fetch itself, and a cross-origin-isolated https page hard-
+	//! blocks mixed (http://) subresources, so an http install URL is
+	//! rejected before the request is ever sent. The R2 custom domain
+	//! serves https directly. (The native engine historically used http
+	//! here because its bundled httplib has no OpenSSL and relied on
+	//! HTTPUtil::BumpToSecureProtocol once httpfs was loaded — that whole
+	//! bootstrap does not exist in wasm, where fetch/XHR handle TLS, so the
+	//! native rationale for http:// simply does not apply to this build.)
+	//!
+	//! Either way the binaries are RSA-signature-verified against the
+	//! embedded HAYBARN_TRUST_ROOT key on load, so transport security is
+	//! defense-in-depth rather than the trust anchor. Core and community
+	//! both resolve under the single haybarn-extensions.query.farm host,
+	//! split by the /core and /community path prefixes.
+	static constexpr const char *CORE_REPOSITORY_URL = "https://haybarn-extensions.query.farm/core";
+	static constexpr const char *COMMUNITY_REPOSITORY_URL = "https://haybarn-extensions.query.farm/community";

 	//! Debugging repositories (target local, relative paths that are produced by DuckDB's build system)
 	static constexpr const char *BUILD_DEBUG_REPOSITORY_PATH = "./build/debug/repository";
